<https://example.org/wikigraph/snapshot/wikipedia/17519/1372885491> <https://example.org/wikigraph/text> "American computer programmer (born 1954) This article's lead section may be too short to adequately summarize the key points . Please consider expanding the lead to provide an accessible overview of all important aspects of the article. ( July 2023 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Larry Wall Wall in 2007 Born Larry Arnold Wall ( 1954-09-27 ) September 27, 1954 (age 71) Los Angeles, California , US Education Seattle Pacific University UC Berkeley Occupations Computer programmer, author Known for Perl , patch , Raku Spouse Gloria Wall Children 4, including Aron Website www .wall .org /~larry / Larry Arnold Wall (born September 27, 1954) is an American computer programmer , linguist, and author known for creating the Perl programming language and the patch tool. ^ \"The man behind the Perl - Things you might not know about Larry Wall\" . blog.builtinperl.com . Archived from the original on February 28, 2018 . Retrieved June 19, 2017 ." .
