<https://example.org/wikigraph/snapshot/wikipedia/93548/1371988525> <https://example.org/wikigraph/text> "English computer scientist Edgar \"Ted\" Codd Born Edgar Frank Codd ( 1923-08-19 ) 19 August 1923 Fortuneswell , Dorset , England Died 18 April 2003 (2003-04-18) (aged 79) Williams Island , Aventura, Florida , USA Education Exeter College, Oxford ( BA ) University of Michigan ( MA , PhD ) Known for Alpha language Database normalization OLAP Relational model Codd's cellular automaton Codd's theorem Codd's 12 rules Boyce–Codd normal form Awards Turing Award (1981) Scientific career Fields Computer Science Workplaces University of Oxford University of Michigan IBM Thesis Propagation, Computation, and Construction in Two-dimensional cellular spaces (1965) Doctoral advisor John Henry Holland Edgar Frank \" Ted \" Codd (19 August 1923 – 18 April 2003) was a British computer scientist who, while working for IBM , invented the relational model for database management, the theoretical basis for relational databases and relational database management systems . He won the 1981 ACM Turing Award . ^ Edgar F. Codd at the Mathematics Genealogy Project ^ Cite error: The named reference ACM Turing was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ \"12 simple rules: How Ted Codd transformed the humble database\" . The Register . Retrieved 19 August 2013 . ^ Codd, Edgar Frank (1982). \"Relational database: A practical foundation for productivity\" . Communications of the ACM . 25 (2): 109– 117. doi : 10.1145/358396.358400 . ^ Edgar Frank Codd at DBLP Bibliography Server ^ Edgar F. Codd author profile page at the ACM Digital Library" .
